@jogehrs Also not sure why you say it has lack of ventilation. The London Underground uses ventilation to exchange air. It's jut not helping.
[->] @jogehrs The only question here is really if railway + human heat generation + heat from the sun from the glass roof &lt; heat removed by ventilation into tunnels + conduction to the surrounding environment. The DB people think the answer is yes, I'm highly sceptical.
[->] @jogehrs My bet is, that if the train station ever opens, the first heat wave we are going to hear stories about how the train station is too hot. It's very common for projects started &gt;10 years ago to get the temperature calculations badly wrong. We have the problem constantly in Vienna.
